# Build & Code Quality Rules

When errors, test failures, or build issues occur, follow autonomous agent healing workflows:

## 1. Grind Until Pass (`grinding-until-pass`)

- Run a tight autonomous loop: _Identify failure -> Apply minimal fix -> Re-execute verification -> Repeat_.
- Maximum 10 autonomous iterations before requesting human intervention.
- Never refactor unrelated code when fixing a compiler or test break.

## 2. Continuous Type Checking (`auto-type-checking`)

- After editing TypeScript files, run `npx tsc --noEmit` to ensure zero compilation regressions.
- Resolve missing props, nullability checks, and type imports immediately before proceeding.

## 3. Port & Dev Server Management (`detecting-port-conflicts`)

- If Metro or Expo reports `EADDRINUSE` (port 8081 or 19000), identify the blocking process and clear the conflict cleanly.
